## Why This Is Asked

This tests design for guardrails, data isolation, and cost controls in Azure OpenAI deployments, a common advanced requirement for regulated customers.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic safety policy engine
- Prompt redaction and blocking
- API Management routing
- Grounding with versioned KB (Blob + Cognitive Search)
- Per-tenant isolation (Cosmos DB) and quotas
- Telemetry and auditing (Data Lake)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal policy eval
function evaluatePrompt(prompt, policies) {
  for (const p of policies) {
    if (p.types?.some(t => prompt.includes(t))) {
      return {blocked: true, reason: p.reason}
    }
  }
  // simple redact example
  const redacted = prompt.replace(/SSN-\d{4}/g, '[REDACTED_SSN]')
  return {blocked: false, redacted}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement per-tenant billing and quotas at API level?
- How would you test guardrails under burst traffic?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end design: IoT ingress, data governance, model integration, privacy controls, and scalable user access governance. It probes architectural decisions, trade-offs, and verification strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Azure IoT Hub ingestion and event-driven processing
- Data Lake Gen2 storage for raw and structured telemetry
- Vector store for embeddings and scheduled refresh cadence
- API Management with per-tenant quotas and private networking to Azure OpenAI
- Purview for data lineage and governance
- Data residency, PII redaction, and security testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js snippet: per-tenant quota check in Azure Functions
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  // fetch quota from a store (e.g., Cosmos Redis cache)
  const quota = await getQuota(tenant);
  if (quota.remaining <= 0) {
    context.res = { status: 429, body: 'Quota exhausted' };
    return;
  }
  await consumeOne(tenant);
  context.res = { status: 200, body: 'ok' };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test latency under burst IoT traffic while preserving data residency?
- What strategies ensure embeddings stay up-to-date without leaking sensitive telemetry to the model?

Why This Is Asked

Assess the ability to design a compliant, multi-tenant AI service on Azure with strong data isolation, governance, and cost controls.


## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation across storage, prompts, and model deployments
- Data governance and lineage with Purview
- PII handling and privacy-by-design in prompts
- Cost controls and API Management gating


## Code Example

```javascript
// Tenant routing sketch
function routeForTenant(req) {
  const tenant = req.headers['X-Tenant'];
  if (!tenant) throw new Error('Missing tenant');
  return {
    deployment: `openai-${tenant}`,
    container: `cosmos-${tenant}`
  };
}
```


